  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Bold Market",
    "overview": "ScootMeal looks like a good stall front: clean cream and white surfaces, confident near-black lettering, and one loud turmeric sign that tells you where to go next. The palette comes straight from the food it sells: turmeric, chili, banana-leaf herb green, and kopi-dark ink. It is warm without being cute, and decisive without being loud everywhere at once.\n\nDensity is medium and phone-first. Screens are built from white cards on a warm off-white page, pill-shaped chips and buttons, round icon buttons, and food photography in circles and soft rectangles. Plus Jakarta Sans carries everything, from the 800-weight headlines to 11px tab labels; hierarchy comes from weight and size, not from a second typeface. Motion is small and physical: presses shrink slightly and spring back, lists fade up in a short stagger, the active tab icon pops. All of it collapses to instant when the OS asks for reduced motion.\n\nThe customer app wears turmeric (its icon and splash are turmeric); the merchant app wears ink (its icon is ink, and it leans on dark surfaces for counter-side alerts). Both apps share this one system and one theme file. The web admin is a plain staff tool that borrows the same ink, cream, line and amber values as CSS variables.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Warm off-white page (`bg`), white cards, hairline warm-grey borders.",
      "Ink for text, dark buttons, active chips and the floating cart bar.",
      "Turmeric reserved for the one main action per screen, the raised Assistant tab and the round \"+\" on dishes.",
      "Pills everywhere: buttons, chips, badges, the cart bar.",
      "One typeface, Plus Jakarta Sans, in five weights.",
      "Soft, warm-tinted shadows (ink at 5–22% opacity), never grey or black."
    ],
    "rules": [
