        "body": "Each screen has at most one turmeric call to action. Everything else is an ink, outline or text button. The raised Assistant tab and the small \"+\" add buttons are the only standing exceptions.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Dark-Tone Text Rule",
        "body": "Turmeric, chili, stone and herb-light are for icons, fills and large shapes. Small text uses the text tones: `amber-text`, `chili-text`, `stone-text`, `herb`.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Category-Grid Rule",
        "body": "The bright `icon-*` colours live only on the Home category icons. They never become buttons, badges or text.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Family Rule",
        "body": "Plus Jakarta Sans only. Contrast comes from weight (400 to 800) and size, never from a second typeface. The theme's `serif` token names are legacy and point at Plus Jakarta Sans regular and medium.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Amber Price Rule",
        "body": "Prices are always bold and always `amber-text`, so \"how much\" is findable at a glance on every card.",
        "section": "typography"
